{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualSES","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SelfDualSES","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.LongExactSequence","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Projection","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.isAntiSelfDual_iff_negated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.isAntiSelfDual_iff_negated","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L205-L206","doc":"Likewise `IsAntiSelfDual` is `IsOdd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.isSelfDual_iff_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.isSelfDual_iff_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L200-L203","doc":"`IsSelfDual` for an involution **is** `BarGradedCollapse.IsEven` for it —\ndefinitionally, once the two are pointed at the same map. Recorded so the\nidentification is checkable rather than asserted in prose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.isSelfDual_iff_minus_component_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.isSelfDual_iff_minus_component_zero","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L173-L191","doc":"**The instanton condition.** A curvature is self-dual exactly when its\nanti-self-dual component vanishes — `F⁻ = 0`, in the block's notation.\n\nWith the splitting in hand this is a statement about the decomposition\nrather than a definition, which is the point of proving the splitting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.quotMinusEquivPlus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.quotMinusEquivPlus","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L164-L171","doc":"**The block's arrow, identified.** `Ω²(A) ⧸ Ω⁻(A) ≅ Ω⁺(A)`.\n\nThis is what `Ω²(A) → Ω⁺(A)` in `rem:self-dual-ses` *means*: the map is the\nquotient by the anti-self-dual part, and it lands isomorphically on the\nself-dual part only because the two are complementary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.isCompl_plus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.isCompl_plus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L159-L162","doc":"`Ω⁺` and `Ω⁻` are complementary: `Ω²(A) = Ω⁺(A) ⊕ Ω⁻(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.codisjoint_plus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.codisjoint_plus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L142-L157","doc":"**The splitting**, and the only place `2` is inverted: `x` is the sum of\nits halves. Over `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` this step is unavailable — the units of\n`ℤ[ℤ]` are `±q^n` and `2` is not among them — which is exactly why\n`rem:self-dual-ses`'s second sentence moves to the archimedean\nrealisation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.sub_star_mem_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.sub_star_mem_minus","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L131-L136","doc":"`x − ⋆x` is anti-self-dual — the unnormalised projector onto `Ω⁻`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.add_star_mem_plus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.add_star_mem_plus","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L124-L129","doc":"`x + ⋆x` is self-dual — the unnormalised projector onto `Ω⁺`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.disjoint_plus_minus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.disjoint_plus_minus","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L117-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.eq_zero_of_selfDual_and_antiSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.eq_zero_of_selfDual_and_antiSelfDual","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L103-L115","doc":"**Self-dual and anti-self-dual meet only at zero** — given no 2-torsion.\n\n`x = ⋆x = −x` gives `x + x = 0`, and nothing more without a hypothesis:\nover a ring of characteristic 2 the two parts coincide. This is\n`BarGradedCollapse.eq_zero_of_even_and_odd` for `⋆_q` instead of the bar\ninvolution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.minus_ses_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.minus_ses_exact","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L95-L101","doc":"**Exactness is free.** The sequence `0 → M⁻ → M → M ⧸ M⁻ → 0` is exact for\n*any* submodule — no involution, no hypothesis on `R`. Recorded first\nprecisely so that it is clear the content of the block is not here: writing\nan exact sequence down is not evidence about the decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.mem_minusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.mem_minusPart","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L92-L93","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.mem_plusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.mem_plusPart","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L89-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.IsAntiSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.IsAntiSelfDual","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L85-L87","doc":"Anti-self-dual: `⋆x = −x`. `F⁻ = 0` is the statement that the curvature's\ncomponent here vanishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.IsSelfDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.IsSelfDual","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L81-L83","doc":"Self-dual: `⋆x = x`. The instanton condition of\n`def:categorical-instanton` is that the curvature lies here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.minusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.minusPart","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L78-L79","doc":"`Ω⁻`: the anti-self-dual part, `ker(⋆ + id)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.plusPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.plusPart","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L75-L76","doc":"`Ω⁺`: the self-dual part, `ker(⋆ − id)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution.star_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution.star_star","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L71-L71","doc":"It squares to the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution.star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution.star","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SelfDualSES.Involution","kind":"structure","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/SelfDualSES.lean#L61-L71","doc":"**An involution** on an `R`-module: `⋆ ∘ ⋆ = id`.\n\nThe `q`-Hodge star of `def:q-hodge-star` at the module level. Carried as a\nstructure rather than a `Prop` on a fixed map so that a module can hold\nmore than one — the corpus has both `⋆_q` and the bar involution. ","signatureChunk":0}]}